    "lawCode": "Amd §1612, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5828\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to qualified capital\ninvestments at relocated vendor tracks in Sullivan county\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nThis bill will facilitate the investment of over six hundred million\ndollars for capital improvements at and adjacent to the Monticello\nRace Track.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 of the bill amends clause (G) of subparagraph (ii) of\nparagraph 1 of subdivision b of section 1612 of the tax law as amended\nby section 1 of part O-1 of chapter 57 of the laws of 2009.  The\nnumber of permanent employees to be hired is reduced from 2,000 to no\nfewer than 1,000. The \"Qualified Capital Investment\" is reduced from\none billion to six hundred million dollars. The construction of the\nConvention Center has been removed from the project leaving \"at least\none eighteen hole golf course, and the construction and issuance of\ncertificates of occupancy for hotels, lodging, spas, dining, retail\nand entertainment venues, parking garages and other capital\nimprovements at or adjacent to the licensed video gaming facility or\nlicensed vendor track.\"\nSection 2 of the bill provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nDue to the economic crisis which severely impacted the banking\nindustry last fall and which continues to today, the ability of the\ndeveloper to secure financing for the project at the previous\nthreshold was impacted. The developer has firm commitments for\nfinancing at six hundred million dollars.  Approval of this\nlegislation will allow the developer to begin construction on the\nproject at this lower level of financing. This bill will facilitate\nthe investment of over $ 600 million dollars for capital improvements\nat and adjacent to the Monticello Race Track. In particular, this bill\nwill support the development of a hotel and golf course at the former\nsite of the Concord Hotel. This bill therefore will help to revitalize\nthe Catskill region by providing at least 1,000 full-time permanent\njobs, as well as thousands of construction-related jobs during the\nconstruction period. Moreover, this bill will guarantee a stream\nfunding to education that will double the current VLT revenues at\nMonticello Race Track.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNo negative fiscal impact to the State but it is anticipated the tax\nreceipts will enhance State and local revenue.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
